        "title": "Draft: add CLI catalog views",
        "body": "## Summary\n\nDraft review PR for the CLI catalog effort described in the RFC: https://github.com/giodl73-repo/rfcs/blob/codex/cli-catalog-overlay-rfc/rfcs/0010-cli-catalog-overlay.md\n\nThis adds a read-only catalog view over existing OpenClaw command/tool surfaces rather than a second command system. It covers:\n\n- `openclaw catalog list` JSON/Markdown output\n- runtime command and plugin descriptor lenses\n- prompt projection from catalog metadata\n- audit, test-matrix, and operator summary views\n- schema fixtures, generated docs, and advisory report artifacts\n- plugin descriptor catalog metadata preservation through registry normalization\n\nThe goal is to make commands, routed operations, plugin commands, prompt-visible surfaces, audit views, and operator/test planning easier to inspect and discuss from one place.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/plugins/captured-registration.test.ts src/plugins/loader.cli-metadata.test.ts src/cli-catalog-overlay/plugin-commands.test.ts`\n- `git diff --check`\n- `codex review --uncommitted`\n\nEarlier focused validation for the six-PR stack also covered catalog list, prompt projection, schema fixtures, generated docs, advisory reports, operator summary, and consumer contract tests.\n\n## Notes\n\nThis is opened as a draft so maintainers can comment on direction, API shape, docs, and whether this should remain one review PR or be split into the six smaller stacked branches already pushed to the fork.",
